Saul and his sons fallen on Mount Gilboa. 9And they stripped him and took
his head and his armor, and sent messengers throughout the land of the
Philistines to carry the good news to their idols and to the people. 10And
they put his armor in the temple of their gods and fastened his head in the
temple of Dagon. 11[†]But when all Jabesh-gilead heard all that the
Philistines had done to Saul, 12all the valiant men arose and took away the
body of Saul and the bodies of his sons, and brought them to Jabesh. And
they buried their bones under the oak in Jabesh and fasted seven days.
13[†]So Saul died a for his breach of faith. He broke faith with the LORD
in that he did not keep the command of the LORD, and also b consulted a
medium, seeking guidance. 14He c did not seek guidance from the LORD.
Therefore the LORD put him to death and d turned the kingdom over to
David the son of Jesse.
